  "question": {
    "html": "<p>S<sub>1</sub> and S<sub>2</sub> are two coherent sound sources with no phase difference. The wavelength of both waves is 0.20 m. P is a point 6.0 m away from S<sub>1</sub> and 6.5 m away from S<sub>2</sub> respectively. At P the amplitude of the wave from S<sub>1</sub> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{0}\"></span> and from S<sub>2</sub> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2x_{0}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the resultant amplitude at P?<br/><br/></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{0}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2x_{0}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3x_{0}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
